    { "key": "sscen.ch.p1_field.title", "value": "The Chief of Heochang Plain" },
    { "key": "sscen.ch.p1_field.blurb", "value": "Scout the plain with the scout. The Yellow Sash chief's camp has weapons from other eras mixed in." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field1.0", "value": "Weapons I have never seen have entered the Yellow Sash chief's camp lately. Ashen rats leap about, and small eye-like things float in the sky." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field1.1", "value": "Eye-like things? Scouting beasts?" },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field1.2", "value": "Not beasts - flying scraps of iron. If we do not clear the plain, we cannot get near the chief." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field1.3", "value": "First I clear the plain, then I see the chief's head." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field2.0", "value": "The chief has fallen! A blue shard of light came out of the middle of the camp, and I do not know who left it." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field2.1", "value": "A bandit could never own such weapons unless someone supplied them." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.field2.2", "value": "Now go and find the teacher. Anyone who has seen more than ten sunsets is fit to learn." },
    { "key": "sscen.ch.p1_job.title", "value": "The First Teacher" },
    { "key": "sscen.ch.p1_job.blurb", "value": "Learn your first class from the teacher. \"The one without a name learns fastest.\"" },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job1.0", "value": "The one without a name learns fastest. Because there is no name to hold you back." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job1.1", "value": "Look at that target. I do not know who set it up, but it is made of wood that does not belong to this land. My weapon is the same. I do not know what age it is from." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job1.2", "value": "🥋 Open the martial window and pick your path. Warrior, archer, wanderer, mystic - the path you choose becomes your first name." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job2.0", "value": "You have chosen. Now, nameless as you are, you have gained a branch." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job2.1", "value": "They say an iron ship hangs at the eastern Gangneung pier, and a traveler photographs it. Go meet that traveler." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.job2.2", "value": "I will go. I will find my name along the way." },
    { "key": "sscen.ch.p3_labyrinth.title", "value": "Memory of the Labyrinth" },
    { "key": "sscen.ch.p3_labyrinth.blurb", "value": "Ieum opens the five-floor labyrinth. Strike down the gate guardian and a lost memory shard may drop - the drifter also fell from the gate." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab1.0", "value": "I open the labyrinth with my exploration lamp. These floors are shells of memory left by the gate. Where you see signs embedded in stone footholds, that is a trace of another age." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab1.1", "value": "If you fell the floor-5 guardian, a lost piece may appear. Even if you leave midway, the shards you gained remain." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab1.2", "value": "If the reason I have no name is there, I must go." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab2.0", "value": "…I remember. I came from beyond the gate. When it opened I fell and landed in this land." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab2.1", "value": "So that is why you had no name. There must be a name you left beyond the gate." },
    { "key": "sscen.scene.lab2.2", "value": "I will go to the gate to find it. Before the Ashen Envoy does." },
